WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.079
Between 2007 and 2010, the Public Sector Integrity Commissioner received two hundred and twenty-eight disclosures.

00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:09.454
Commissioner Ouimet investigated seven.

00:00:09.454 --> 00:00:12.125
Founded cases of wrongdoing: zero.

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:18.034
The maximum reprisal compensation under the Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act is ten thousand dollars.

00:00:18.034 --> 00:00:23.386
Vice-Admiral Mark Norman: charged, then charges stayed in May 2019.

00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:27.056
The government spent one point four million dollars fighting disclosure.

00:00:27.056 --> 00:00:33.568
Richard Colvin sent seventeen memos warning of Afghan detainee torture — and was attacked by his own government for it.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:40.136
In the United States, the False Claims Act has recovered over seventy-two billion dollars since 1987.

00:00:40.136 --> 00:00:42.693
Canada's equivalent has recovered zero.

00:00:42.693 --> 00:00:45.124
The system does not protect whistleblowers.

00:00:45.124 --> 00:00:46.295
It punishes them.
